    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through our Funds-in-Trust (FiT) program, Australia works with the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) to raise awareness in our region of the rights and responsibilities derived from international intellectual property rules, including their link to regional trade and investment and regional and global trade architecture. The program supported 16 women entrepreneurs from 9 Pacific island countries &#x2013; Fiji, Kiribati, Niue, Palau, Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Solomon Islands, and Vanuatu &#x2013; to better understand international intellectual property principles, systems, and tools as they relate to traditional knowledge and traditional cultural expressions. It highlighted the value and challenges of intellectual property in supporting Pacific businesses and projects.</narrative>
